NAME
       getty - log in on a text console

SYNOPSIS
       getty [--noclear] ttyN

DESCRIPTION
       getty opens /dev/ttyN, makes it standard input, output and error,
       prints /etc/issue (or a default banner) and asks for a user name and
       a password. The password is checked against /etc/shadow. On success
       getty switches to the user's uid and gid, changes to the home
       directory, prints /etc/motd and starts the login shell from
       /etc/passwd.

       On a live system without /etc/shadow any name logs in as root.

       After three wrong passwords getty exits and init(8) starts a new one.
       In /etc/issue \n is replaced by the host name and \l by the tty name.

OPTIONS
       --noclear
           do not clear the screen first (used on tty1 to keep the boot log)

FILES
       /etc/issue, /etc/motd, /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow

SEE ALSO
       init(8), chvt(1)
